UPDATE companies SET description='Electrical Contractors Hawaii, Inc. (ECH) was founded in 1998 on the island of Oahu, with its headquarters in Kapolei, Hawaii. The company began as a high‑voltage electrical contractor focused on federal military projects, installing substations, communications, CATV, and overhead and underground distribution systems. It is a service‑disabled veteran‑owned small business (SDVOSB).

ECH provides full‑service electrical construction, installation, and maintenance for military, government, industrial, commercial, and residential projects. Its services cover electrical substations, switchgear, communications infrastructure, fiber optics, CATV, high‑voltage and medium‑voltage work, underground and overhead distribution, runway and highway lighting, building and historical renovations, pump stations, sewer lift stations, fitness centers, and office buildings. The firm also offers electrical design consulting, value engineering, and 24‑hour emergency service. ECH employs 50–100 electricians, linemen, groundmen, and support staff, and holds C‑10, C‑62, and C‑63 licenses in Hawaii plus a General Building and C‑13 electrical license in California and Arizona.

The company’s primary customers are U.S. military branches — Army, Navy, Air Force — and federal and state government agencies. Notable projects include electrical work at Pearl Harbor, Kaneohe Marine Corps Base, Camp Pendleton, Twenty‑Nine Palms, Hanscom AFB in Massachusetts, the Kahuku Wind Farm, Onizuka Village, Capehart/Earhart Military Housing, Ford Island, and the Red Hill Mauka project. ECH also serves commercial and industrial clients such as pump stations, sewer lift stations, airport hangars, and office buildings.

ECH emphasizes a zero‑accident safety culture, earning the Associated Builders and Contractors Platinum Safety Award eight of nine years from 2003 to 2011 and multiple Excellence in Construction Grand Awards for work on military installations. The firm highlights attention to detail, dedication to quality, and an experienced supervisory workforce as key differentiators.', certifications=ARRAY['SDVOSB','HUBZone Applied']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Electrical substation installation", "Communications wiring and terminations", "CATV cabling and installation", "Electrical distribution systems", "Highway lighting", "Distribution upgrades", "Overhead pole and line construction", "Switchgear installation and maintenance", "Communications infrastructure", "Fiber optic cable installation", "Medium and high voltage work", "Underground installations", "Building and historical renovations", "Runway lighting", "Transformer installation and testing", "Pump station electrical work", "Airport hangar electrical work", "Sewer lift station electrical work", "Fitness center electrical work", "High\u2011bay lighting", "Office building electrical work", "Electrical consulting", "Value engineering", "Electrical design services", "Plans and specifications", "Complete electrical engineering services", "Maintenance contracts", "Breaker and panel change\u2011out", "24\u2011hour emergency work", "Electrical troubleshooting", "Tenant improvements"], "industries": ["Military", "Government", "Industrial", "Commercial", "Residential"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["SDVOSB (Service\u2011Disabled Veteran\u2011Owned Small Business) certification", "Zero\u2011accident safety record with ABC Platinum Safety Award (8 of 9 years, 2003\u20132011)", "Holds C\u201110, C\u201162, C\u201163 licenses in Hawaii and General Building/C\u201113 licenses in California and Arizona", "Provides 24\u2011hour emergency electrical service", "Offers electrical design consulting and value engineering"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 1998 -> /about", "Headquarters in Kapolei, Hawaii -> db", "Service-Disabled Veteran-Owned Small Business (SDVOSB) -> / (homepage) and /services", "Employee count 50-100 -> /about", "Licenses: C-10, C-62, C-63 (Hawaii); General Building & C-13 (California, Arizona) -> /services", "Projects: Pearl Harbor, Kaneohe, Camp Pendleton, Twenty-Nine Palms, Hanscom AFB, Kahuku Wind Farm, Onizuka Village, Capehart/Earhart, Ford Island, Red Hill Mauka -> / (homepage) and /about", "Awards: ABC Platinum Safety Award 8 of 9 years 2003-2011; Excellence in Construction Grand Awards multiple years -> /about", "Services list -> /services", "Industries served: military, government, industrial, commercial, residential -> / (homepage)", "HUBZone Applied -> /services"], "company_type": "Installer / service company", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "ECH provides cost-effective, full-service electrical solutions for projects of all sizes.", "founded_year": "1998", "employee_count": "50-100", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Service-disabled veteran-owned", "Small business"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='electrical-contractors-hawaii-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Electrical Controls of Maine is based in Lyman, Maine, and was founded in 2025. The company operates as a New England–focused provider of electrical controls solutions, delivering on-site engineering, maintenance, and consulting services to industrial and municipal clients.

Its service portfolio centers on electrical safety and process efficiency. The firm conducts arc flash analysis and consulting to protect personnel near electrical systems, designs and implements process automation for commercial and industrial facilities, and provides maintenance planning, training, and project management for environments with complex electrical infrastructure. Field services include pump station electrical installation and general on-site engineering support.

The customer base spans public and private organizations across several sectors. Municipal water and wastewater clients include the Portland Water District. The company also collaborates with automation vendors such as Rockwell Automation, Emerson Automation, GE Vernova, Ignition, VT SCADA, Power‑Tronics, ETAP, and SKM.

Electrical Controls of Maine emphasizes long‑term client relationships and a problem‑solving approach that aims to address immediate issues while anticipating future challenges. This philosophy underpins its engagement model across safety analysis, automation, and project delivery.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Arc Flash Analysis", "Process Automation", "Maintenance Planning", "Training", "Project Management", "On-site Engineering & Maintenance Services", "Pump Station Electrical Installation"], "industries": ["Water/Wastewater", "Power Generation", "Paper Manufacturing", "Lumber/Wood Products", "Flotation Technology", "Municipal Government", "Commercial", "Industrial"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Long-term client relationships", "Thinking outside the box to solve current problems and anticipate future challenges", "Arc Flash analysis and consulting for electrical safety", "Process automation for commercial, industrial, and municipal facilities", "Strategic partnerships with major automation vendors (Rockwell Automation, Emerson, GE Vernova, etc.)"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 2025 -> db", "Headquartered in Lyman, Maine -> db", "Provides Arc Flash analysis, process automation, training, project management -> /", "Offers on-site engineering & maintenance services, pump station electrical installation -> /", "Serves clients including Portland Water District, Algonquin Power, Sappi Fine Paper, Red Mill Lumber, Floatation Technologies -> /", "Partners with Rockwell Automation, Emerson Automation, GE Vernova, Ignition, VT SCADA, Power-Tronics, ETAP, SKM -> /", "Emphasizes long-term client relationships and thinking outside the box -> /"], "company_type": "Installer / service company", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "We are a New England based company providing Arc Flash analysis service, process automation, training and project planning and management to indust