UPDATE companies SET description='Electrical Power Products, operating as EP², was founded in the fall of 1988 in Des Moines, Iowa. Terry Nelson envisioned a better way to manufacture high-quality relay and control panels, and was joined by Tom David and Randy Dochterman within months. The three founders started in a 1,200-square-foot leased space with a commitment to quality that remains the company''s highest priority.

Today EP² operates from a 310,000-square-foot facility with over 500 employees. The company produces complete power management systems for commercial and utility markets, including control enclosures, protective relay panels, and control systems for power generation, transmission, and distribution. Its capabilities span metal fabrication, powder coating, component mounting, wiring, and final testing, all governed by a five-point inspection process. The company reports serving 1,041 customers in the power industry.

EP² serves the commercial and utility power sectors, renewable energy facilities such as wind, solar, and geothermal installations, and the growing data center market. Its integrated modular control systems are delivered as "drop-in-place" units ready for immediate operation. The firm''s engineering staff includes IEEE members, project managers, and estimating and procurement specialists.

The company differentiates itself through a quality management system that inspects products at five stages — after metal fabrication, powder coating, component mounting, wiring, and before shipment. Long-term employee retention, with many staff members staying 30-plus years, is cited as a reflection of workplace culture. An overhead crane enables weather-controlled handling of large enclosures, and the company emphasizes modernizing the nation''s power grid and supporting reliable data center power.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Relay & Control Panel manufacturing", "Control enclosure fabrication", "Protective relay panel assembly", "Control systems for power generation, transmission, distribution", "Integrated modular control systems (drop-in-place)", "Metal fabrication", "Powder coating", "Component mounting", "Wiring", "Final inspection and testing", "Contract administration", "Document control", "Material procurement", "Material receiving and inspection", "In-process quality inspections", "Packaging and shipping"], "industries": ["Commercial power", "Utility power", "Renewable energy (wind, solar, geothermal)", "Data centers", "Power generation", "Power transmission", "Power distribution"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["Overhead crane"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Five-stage inspection process covering fabrication, coating, mounting, wiring, and pre-shipment", "\"Drop-in-place\" modular control systems delivered ready for immediate operation", "Overhead crane for weather-controlled enclosure handling", "35+ years focused on relay and control panel manufacturing", "Workforce with 30+ year tenure reflecting organizational stability"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1988 -> /about", "Founders Terry Nelson, Tom David, Randy Dochterman -> /about", "HQ Des Moines, IA -> / (Contact Us) and /about-us", "Facility 310,000 sq ft -> /about-us and /about", "Employees 500+ -> /about-us, /about, and db", "Products: relay panels, control enclosures, control systems -> / (Relay Panels section)", "Industries: commercial, utility, renewable (wind, solar, geothermal), data centers -> / (Renewable Energy Products) and /about", "Quality: five-point inspection process -> /quality", "Overhead crane for enclosure handling -> /about (2007 Expansion)", "1,041 customers in power industry -> / (Electrical Power Products at a Glance)", "Employee retention 30+ years -> /about (Recent Years)", "Modular drop-in-place systems -> / (Integrated Control Systems)"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "EP\u00b2 provides complete power management systems for commercial and utility industries including control enclosures, protective relay panels, and control systems for power generation, transmission, and distribution.", "founded_year": "1988", "employee_count": "500", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='electrical-power-products' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Electro-Mechanical Industries, Inc. (EMI) was founded in 1981 in Plymouth, Minnesota. The company has grown over more than four decades, with a team that spans five generations of industry experience, to become a manufacturer of electrical distribution equipment for national and international markets.

EMI operates a 66,000-square-foot facility where it engineers and manufactures custom low- and medium-voltage switchgear, control and switchgear houses, control panels, wire ways, wall and floor ducts, panel trims, pull boxes, and sheet metal enclosures. The shop also provides retrofit services such as breaker upgrades, ground-fault and phase-loss protection, and custom bus bar fabrication including measurement, punching, and bending of aluminum and copper bar stock.

The company serves electrical contractors, distributors, and integrators across commercial, industrial, mining, mission-critical, and renewable-energy projects. Its technical team assists with code compliance, utility requirements, and field measurements, while in-house engineering allows rapid response to design changes and construction revisions.

EMI’s stated mission is to partner with customers to deliver innovative solutions that meet unique requirements and exceed expectations. The firm emphasizes quick adaptation to project constraints, technical support for evolving codes, and a commitment to making its customers look good through reliable, customized power distribution equipment.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom low-voltage switchgear manufacturing", "Custom medium-voltage switchgear manufacturing", "Control and switchgear house fabrication", "Control panel assembly", "Wire way, wall duct, and floor duct fabrication", "Panel trim and pull box manufacturing", "Sheet metal enclosure fabrication", "Retrofit of main bolted pressure switches", "Breaker upgrade and replacement", "Panel and panelboard retrofit", "Ground fault protection installation", "Phase loss protection installation", "Switchboard control and metering integration", "Custom electrical bus bar measurement and design", "Custom bus bar punching and bending", "Stocked bus bar supply (aluminum and copper)"], "industries": ["Commercial electrical projects", "Industrial electrical projects", "Mining", "Mission critical facilities", "Renewable energy"], "materials": ["Aluminum", "Copper"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Quick adaptation to construction revisions to keep projects on schedule", "In-house engineering and manufacturing for rapid response", "Technical support for code changes and utility requirements", "Custom low- and medium-voltage switchgear design", "Over 45 years of manufacturing experience"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 1981 -> /about", "66,000 sq ft facility in Plymouth, Minnesota -> /about", "Manufacturer of electrical distribution equipment -> /about", "Custom low and medium voltage switchgear -> /about", "Control and switchgear houses, control panels, wire ways, ducts, panel trims, pull boxes -> /about", "Serves electrical contractors, distributors, integrators -> /", "Industries: commercial, industrial, mining, mission critical, renewable energy -> /", "Retrofit services: main bolted pressure switches, breaker upgrades, panel retrofits, ground fault, phase loss protection -> /services", "Custom bus bar measurement, design, punching, bending -> /services", "Stocked bus bar sizes 1/4\u2033 x 2\u2033 thru 1/4\u2033 x 6\u2033 Aluminum or Copper -> /services", "In-house engineering and manufacturing -> /services", "Technical support for code changes, utility requirements -> /", "Quick adaptation to construction revisions -> /", "Mission: partnering to deliver innovative solutions -> /about", "Values: customer focus, integrity, excellence, service, EMI family, innovation -> /about", "Five generations of expertise -> /", "Headquarters: Plymouth, Minnesota -> db", "Company type: Manufacturer (OEM) -> /about", "Materials: Aluminum, Copper -> /services", "45 years of service -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Electro-Mechanical Industries, Inc. (EMI) is a manufacturer of standard electrical distribution equipment serving the needs of the electrical industry in the national and international marketplaces. We are a OEM that specializes in custom low and medium voltage switchgear...", "founded_year": "1981", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='electro-mechanical-industries' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Electron Technologies Corporation (ETC) operates from South Windsor, Connecticut, where it provides irradiation processing services to manufacturers across New England. The company describes itself as a fast-growing irradiation processing provider in the region, serving clients that include large firms in multiple sectors.

ETC offers contract irradiation services that cover the full product development cycle. Its team supports customers from initial research and engineering through testing, processing, and final delivery. The company positions its operation as an extension of the client’s own manufacturing line, handling tasks such as radiation polymerization for coatings and other material modification processes.

The company serves the semiconductor, aerospace, plastics, medical device, and gemstone industries. Its customer base consists of what it calls companies that rely on ETC’s expertise and technology to meet manufacturing goals, including sterilization of medical products and aseptic packaging as well as material enhancement for electronic components.

