UPDATE companies SET description='Electronic Assembly Products (EAP) is a manufacturer''s representative agency based in Dayton, Ohio. Founded in January 2002 by John W. Johnson, the firm began after Johnson''s career at Pioneer Standard Electronics, Marshall Industries, and REStronics Midwest, where he became a partner. Johnson launched EAP to provide technology-electronic assembly products and a high level of service to both customers and suppliers.

The agency operates with a small team of technical salespeople covering territories in Ohio, Michigan, Florida, and beyond.

The company serves industries including electronics assembly, medical device, automotive, contract manufacturing, wiring harness, test and measurement, and military/defense. Customers range from large OEMs such as Rockwell Collins and Panasonic to regional contract manufacturers and MRO buyers. EAP''s representatives have experience with programs such as TCAS and IRIDIUM at Honeywell and have managed global accounts for Denso and Lear.

