UPDATE companies SET description='Electronic Concepts Inc. has operated from Eatontown, New Jersey since its founding in 1969. The veteran-owned small business also maintains a European office in Oughterard, County Galway, Ireland.

The company designs and manufactures film capacitors for energy storage, AC filtering, DC link, coupling/decoupling, snubber, inverter, frequency discriminating, resonant circuit, and high-temperature applications. Its product lines include the LH3 series with low ESL under 10 nH, the EV/HEV series for electric vehicles, and multiple high-temperature series rated above 105 °C. In-house capabilities span dielectric research, film capacitor manufacturing, testing, and a design center that offers application notes, technical papers, and interactive formula calculators. The firm also performs contract R&D for universities, private institutions, and government laboratories.

Electronic Concepts serves the aerospace sector (AS9100D certified), power electronics, electric vehicle, industrial power supply, and research communities. Its capacitors appear in inverter applications, resonant power circuits, switching power supplies, and high-power filtering. The company exhibits at IEEE ECCE, APEC, and PCIM conferences, and its R&D division collaborates with academic and government labs.

The company emphasizes low-inductance, high-current-carrying capability at elevated temperatures, and offers series or parallel safety options for high-power AC filtering.', certifications=ARRAY['AS9100D','ISO 9001:2015','ISO 14001:2015','ISO 45001:2018','DPRV Certified','UL Recognized']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Film capacitor manufacturing", "Dielectric research", "Contract R&D", "Testing services", "Shop capabilities", "Film capacitor design center", "In-stock inventory", "Technical documentation (application notes, technical papers, glossary, interactive formula calculators)"], "industries": ["Aerospace", "Power electronics", "Electric vehicle (EV/HEV)", "Industrial power supplies", "Research institutions"], "materials": ["Metallized film", "Film dielectric"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Low inductance with high current carrying capability", "High power AC filtering with series or parallel safety options", "Capacitors rated for operating temperatures above 105 \u00b0C", "Contract R&D for universities, private institutions, and government labs", "Veteran-owned small business with AS9100D and ISO 9001/14001/45001 certifications"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1969 -> homepage footer ''Proudly Serving You Since 1969''", "Headquarters Eatontown, NJ -> homepage address ''526 Industrial Way W. | Eatontown, New Jersey 07724''", "Veteran-owned, Small business -> homepage footer ''Veteran Owned'', ''Small Business''", "Certifications AS9100D, ISO 9001:2015, ISO 14001:2015, ISO 45001:2018, DPRV Certified, UL Recognized -> homepage footer", "Product lines LH3, EV/HEV, high-temperature series -> homepage product listings", "Capabilities: manufacturing, testing, shop, dielectric research, R&D, design center -> homepage menu", "Industries: aerospace (AS9100D), power electronics (IEEE ECCE, APEC, PCIM), EV/HEV, research institutions -> homepage conferences and R&D description", "Low inductance, high current, high temperature >105\u00b0C -> homepage product descriptions"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Electronic Concepts Inc. - Film Capacitor Manufacturer", "founded_year": "1969", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Veteran-owned", "Small business"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='electronic-concepts-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Electronic Connections Inc is a privately held electronics distributor headquartered in Myrtle Beach, South Carolina, with a second location in Manchester Township, New Jersey. The company was founded in 1994 by Steve Jordan, who established the business on a philosophy of total customer satisfaction.

The firm stocks and supplies interconnect, passive, and electro‑mechanical components from more than 200 authorized product lines. Beyond distribution, it provides value‑added services including custom labeling and marking, custom component and connector modification and assembly, custom DIN‑rail design and assembly, and cable assembly technology.

Electronic Connections serves primarily the aerospace and defense sectors. Its authorized lines include products from Bendix (Amphenol Aerospace), ITT Cannon, Deutsch Defense/Aerospace, Positronic Industries, and Harbour Industries, among others, indicating a customer base of aerospace and defense manufacturers and contractors.

