UPDATE companies SET description='Empire Metal Products was founded in 2004 in Phoenix, Arizona. The company operates two campuses in the city — a North Campus focused on commercial HVAC and a South Campus handling residential HVAC, curbs, and custom fabrication — along with an East Valley pickup location at AAA A/C Supply in Mesa.

The shop produces HVAC sheet metal (duct, spiral, fittings, transitions), roof curbs and adapters, and custom welded fabrications including structural components, platforms, brackets, racks, and assemblies. Processes cover cutting, bending, punching, welding, lock-seam and spiral duct fabrication, coil-line production, and pre-fab assembly with taps and fittings installed. The combined facilities span 80,000 square feet with 150-plus employees, processing over four million pounds of metal annually and serving more than 600 contractors.

Primary customers are HVAC and mechanical contractors across Arizona, from commercial and residential projects to specialized needs such as restaurant stainless wall panels, mini-split displays, truck and trailer fabrication, and material-handling carts. The company also supports contractors with daily delivery routes throughout Phoenix and freight options for wider distribution.

Empire emphasizes a fabricator-first mindset: verifying dimensions and unusual conditions before production, labeling orders for easier staging, and maintaining clear communication so questions are resolved before parts hit the floor. The approach grew from early contractor requests for faster duct packages, cleaner curb changeouts, and heavier custom assemblies, building a reputation on work that fits when it reaches the field.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["HVAC sheet metal fabrication (duct, spiral, fittings, transitions)", "Custom metal fabrication and welding", "Roof curb and adapter manufacturing", "Lock-seam duct fabrication (galvanized, stainless, aluminum)", "Spiral duct and fitting fabrication", "Structural welding (platforms, brackets, racks, assemblies)", "Pre-fab duct assembly with taps and fittings installed", "Coil-line production", "Cutting, bending, punching", "Shop drawing creation and design refinement", "Delivery services (local routes and freight)", "East Valley pickup (Mesa)"], "industries": ["HVAC contractors", "Mechanical contractors", "Commercial construction", "Residential construction", "Sheet metal contractors"], "materials": ["Galvanized steel", "Stainless steel", "Aluminum"], "equipment": ["Coil line"], "volume": "One-off to 4M+ lbs per year", "lead_time": "Same-day pickup available for East Valley orders (order AM, pickup PM); typical lead times communicated per order", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Same-day East Valley pickup (order AM, pickup PM) for orders placed before cutoff", "Real-time verification of dimensions, openings, and unusual conditions before fabrication", "Labeled and staged orders to simplify field installation", "Daily local delivery routes plus freight options across Arizona", "Coil-line production for faster output without sacrificing fit or consistency"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 2004 -> / (About section)", "Two Phoenix campuses (North and South) and East Valley pickup in Mesa -> / (Two Phoenix Campuses section)", "80,000 sq ft shop space, 150+ employees, 4M+ lbs/year -> / (Capacity that supports real schedules)", "600+ contractors served -> / (Homepage metrics)", "HVAC sheet metal, curbs & adapters, custom fab & welding -> / (Services section)", "Coil-line production for faster output -> / (Custom Fabrication Capabilities)", "Daily delivery routes + freight options -> / (Delivery & Pickup)", "Materials: galvanized steel, stainless steel, aluminum -> / (Product list)", "Same-day East Valley pickup (Order AM \u2192 Pickup PM) -> / (East Valley Pickup)", "Verification of dimensions and openings before fabrication -> / (How we help)", "Labeled orders for easier staging -> / (What You Can Expect)", "Pre-fab duct assemblies with taps and fittings installed -> / (Custom Fabrication Capabilities)"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "HVAC sheet metal, curbs and adapters, and custom fabrication built by people who answer the phone, catch problems early, and stand behind the work.", "founded_year": "2004", "employee_count": "150+", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='empire-metal-products' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Empire Precision Plastics operates from Rochester, New York, where it was founded in 1992. The company is led by Chief Executive Officer Joe Buonocore, who began his career as a machine operator and later held profit-and-loss responsibility for a global injection molding business.

The nearly 70,000-square-foot facility houses 50 late-model electric and hydraulic injection molding machines, nearly 80 percent of which are automated. An in-house tool shop supports full-service mold design and build. Core processes include scientific injection molding, white-room molding and assembly, polymer optics molding, MuCell microcellular foaming, thermoplastic elastomer insert and over-molding, multi-component (two-shot) molding, and high-heat engineering material processing. Downstream assembly capabilities encompass ultrasonic welding, heat staking, machining, pad printing, and electro-optical assembly, with work cells integrated into the molding cycle.

The company serves medical and healthcare, military and defense, aerospace, industrial, optics, polymer optics, consumer electronics, and firearms sectors. Customers range from OEMs requiring production-intent prototypes to those transferring existing production tools for high-volume manufacturing.

