UPDATE companies SET description='Enable Injections, Inc. was founded in 2010 by medical device entrepreneur Mike Hooven in Cincinnati, Ohio. Hooven, who previously founded AtriCure and Enable Medical, established the company to develop a wearable drug delivery platform that could administer large volumes of medication subcutaneously.

The company designs, develops, and manufactures the enFuse® system, a purely mechanical, hands-free wearable injector that delivers pharmaceutical and biologic therapeutics subcutaneously. The platform accommodates drug product viscosities ranging from 1 to 100 centipoise and eliminates the need for intravenous infusion, allowing patients to receive treatment through a simple injection under the skin. All design, development, and manufacturing operations are based at the company''s Cincinnati headquarters.

Enable Injections serves the pharmaceutical and biotechnology industries, partnering with companies such as Sanofi, Sobi, and Aptar Digital Health to integrate enFuse with specific therapies. Sanofi’s subcutaneous Sarclisa (iscatuximab) has received regulatory approval in the U.S. and EU for administration via enFuse, while Sobi’s Aspaveli (pegcetacoplan) has obtained CE certification for use with the platform. The company also supports clinical trials and commercial launch planning for partnered combination products.

The company states its technology was driven by patient insights to improve the treatment experience, increase safety, and reduce the time, cost, and burden of chronic disease management. By removing needle-stick hazards and manual mixing steps, enFuse aims to enable patients to perform light to moderate activities during administration. The platform has been recognized by industry publications including Fierce Pharma and PM360 for its novel approach to large-volume subcutaneous delivery.', certifications=ARRAY['CE Certification']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Wearable drug delivery platform development", "Subcutaneous injection system manufacturing", "Mechanical hands-free injection technology", "Fill technology for biologics", "Combination product development", "Clinical trial support", "Regulatory submission support"], "industries": ["Pharmaceutical", "Biotechnology", "Medical Device", "Healthcare", "Combination Products"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Purely mechanical, hands-free wearable injector for large-volume subcutaneous delivery", "Compatible with drug product viscosities from 1 to 100 cP", "Eliminates needle-stick hazards and drug exposure from manual mixing", "Allows patients to perform light to moderate activities during administration", "CE certified for use with Aspaveli (pegcetacoplan) distributed by Sobi"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 2010 -> /about", "Founder Mike Hooven -> /about", "Headquartered in Cincinnati, Ohio -> /about", "More than $300 million in capital funding -> /about", "Develops and manufactures enFuse wearable drug delivery platform -> /about", "enFuse is purely mechanical hands-free wearable technology for subcutaneous delivery -> /about", "Compatible with viscosities 1-100 cP -> /", "Partnerships with Sanofi, Sobi, Aptar Digital Health -> /", "CE Certification for enFuse with Aspaveli -> /", "Recognized by Fierce Pharma and PM360 -> /", "Removes needle stic