UPDATE companies SET description='Based in Baltimore, Maryland, Maryland Junkyards has operated for more than three decades as a network of five salvage yards across the state. The company''s locations include Erdman Auto Parts on Erdman Avenue in Baltimore, Redmonds Auto Parts in Pasadena, Marty''s Auto Parts on Hollins Ferry Road, A-1 Auto Sales in Havre de Grace, and Stokes Auto Parts in Jefferson.

The business centers on used auto parts, automotive repair, towing, and vehicle recycling. Across its five facilities, the company stocks millions of parts covering most makes and models of cars and trucks, and offers installation services. Each year it recycles approximately 75,000 gallons of gasoline recovered from salvaged vehicles, using the filtered fuel in its own fleet and converting engine oils, transmission fluids, and gear lubricants to heat its warehouses; the remaining hulks are shredded for steel.

The company buys junk vehicles directly from the public, providing free towing and cash on the spot, and also sells parts nationally through its eBay storefront.

