UPDATE companies SET description='Everwood Furnishings operates from St Ignatius, Montana, where it handcrafts premium polywood furniture for outdoor living spaces. The company’s founding year and ownership structure are not publicly disclosed, but its focus on domestic manufacturing and recycled materials has defined its operation since inception.

The manufacturer produces outdoor furniture — including gliders, tables, and seating — using poly lumber, a material made from 95 percent recycled plastic such as milk jugs and detergent bottles. Each piece is shaped by hand and assembled with stainless steel fasteners that resist saltwater and weather corrosion. The process yields furniture that does not crack, warp, rot, or fade, and requires no painting or sealing, offering a low‑maintenance alternative to traditional wood.

Everwood sells exclusively through a wholesale network, supplying dealers who serve residential and commercial customers for patios, parks, porches, and other outdoor settings. The company does not sell directly to end consumers, instead directing buyers to its dealer network or downloadable catalog.

The business states its primary aim is to bring glory to God, with customer satisfaction as a secondary goal. It differentiates itself by using 95 percent recycled content, corrosion‑resistant hardware, and a wholesale‑only model that supports dealer partners, positioning itself as part of a “green earth revolution” that repurposes post‑consumer plastic.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Handcrafted furniture assembly", "Poly lumber shaping", "Stainless steel fastening", "Recycled plastic furniture manufacturing"], "industries": ["Outdoor furniture", "Patio furniture", "Park furniture", "Porch furniture", "Wholesale furniture distribution"], "materials": ["Poly lumber (polyethylene)", "Recycled HDPE (milk jugs, detergent bottles)", "Stainless steel fasteners"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["95% recycled content from post\u2011consumer plastic", "Stainless steel fasteners in every piece", "Wholesale\u2011only distribution through dealer network", "Handcrafted assembly in Montana"], "facts_used": ["Location: St Ignatius, Montana -> db", "Product: Premium polywood furniture handcrafted for durability -> /", "Material: 95% recycled content from milk jugs and detergent bottles -> /about-us", "Hardware: Stainless steel fasteners resist corrosion -> /about-us", "Business model: Wholesale only -> /about-us", "Mission: Foremost goal to bring glory to God -> /about-us", "Process: Handcrafted, shaped parts, fastened with stainless steel -> /about-us", "Industries: Outdoor furniture for patios, parks, porches -> /", "No direct-to-consumer sales -> /about-us"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Our outdoor furniture is handcrafted using only high grade weather resistant materials.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='everwood-furnishings' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Evolution Graphix is a small apparel and graphics company based in Hermon, Maine. The business was started by Troy, a civil engineer, and Nikki, a registered nurse, who wanted to own and operate their own company to control quality, customer service, and deadlines. They describe the venture as pursuing the American dream of working for themselves.

The company provides custom decoration and fabrication services including embroidery, sublimation, direct-to-film (DTF) digital printing, decal production, banner and sign printing, custom cornhole board manufacturing, and laser etching.

Their customer base includes fraternal organizations such as the Widows Sons and Anah Shrine, educational institutions like Hermon Hawks for spirit wear, and sports teams such as The Maine Threat. They also run a dedicated Masonic gear site, MasonicME.com, and donate products and time to support fundraising efforts for these groups.

